Package: paq8px
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: experimental lossless data compressor (PAQ8 family)
 paq8px is a context-mixing lossless compressor with very high
 compression ratios, at the cost of speed and memory.
 .
 HERMES stations use it to compress sensor data before sending it over
 HF radio. Archives are only readable by the same paq8px version, so
 every station of a network must run the same package version.
 .
 Built for generic CPUs of each architecture (no -march=native).
